WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Look, AI is not going to replace demand planners, but it will absolutely delete the six hours

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.280
a day you currently waste just finding problems.

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.440
Because think about it, you don't get paid to hunt for exceptions, right?

4
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.360
You could pay to make decisions about them.

5
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.120
So why on earth does finding them take your entire day?

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.040
In a real, live operation, you're dealing with tens of thousands of supply chain events

7
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.440
every single month.

8
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.040
A human literally cannot triage that manually.

9
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.540
It's just impossible.

10
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.660
So what happens?

11
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.240
With way too much data, teams just react to whoever is shouting the loudest.

12
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.240
You end up fixing the loud problem instead of the expensive one that's quietly eating

13
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.740
your margins.

14
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.200
Enter the AI exception brain.

15
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.400
This thing reads every single event, flags exactly what broke, and this is the real

16
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.560
game changer, it ranks those disruptions by actual revenue impact.

17
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.480
So instead of waking up to a totally cluttered dashboard of 5,000 things that might matter,

18
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.380
you just open a ranked list of the 5 things that actually do.

19
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.140
We call this the human supervised agent model.

20
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.100
The AI detects and ranks.

21
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.340
You use your judgment, handle the negotiation, and make the final call.

22
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.460
Nobody gets replaced here.

23
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.060
The boring half just gets deleted.

24
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.060
And this isn't just theory.

25
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.660
Just look at Dubai based demand planner Vinayak Bhadani, who has over 36,000 supply

26
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.740
chain events indexed and managed in his AI system.

27
00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.480
It gives operators insane leverage.

28
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.400
We're talking real time delivery tracking, AI root cause guidance, and exceptions perfectly

29
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.600
ranked way before they ever blow up into massive escalations.

30
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.240
Because here is the ultimate takeaway for this explainer.

31
00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.560
The planner who supervises AI agents is going to out plan the planner who just refreshes

32
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.000
spreadsheets every single time.

33
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.440
So are you going to keep hunting for problems all day, or are you ready to actually

34
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.340
start deciding them?

35
00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.420
It's time to upgrade your operating system by checking out Vinayak Bhadani's work out

36
00:01:59.420 --> 00:01:59.940
of Dubai.
